# WordPress PHP Conventions (ANM)

See `edminboost-anm-compliance.mdc` for the security gate.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package EdminBoost\AdminNoticeManager
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

`uninstall.php` uses `WP_UNINSTALL_PLUGIN` instead of `ABSPATH`.

## Security

- Check capabilities before rendering admin pages: `current_user_can( EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::CAPABILITY )`.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize all settings via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback` in `register_setting()`.
- New AJAX handlers: register in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ajax::register_hooks()`, implement `handle_*`, call `verify_request()` (digest/webhook preview: sanitize nested input with dedicated helpers when accepting unsaved form fields).

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin::run()` or class `register_hooks()` — not in the bootstrap file (except activation/deactivation registration).
- Use Settings API for the main settings option (`register_setting`, `settings_fields`, `submit_button`). Rules/inbox use dedicated classes + AJAX where appropriate.
- Enqueue assets with `EDMINBOOST_ANM_VERSION` as the version string.
- Pass data to JS via `wp_localize_script()` — global `edminboostAnmData` from `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::get_localized_data()`.
- Page slugs: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` with `-inbox`, `-rules`, `-settings` suffixes.
- Inbox list: sanitize GET/POST list args via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::parse_inbox_list_args()`; paginate with `get_inbox_list_slice()` (20 per page). `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox::query()` honors `page` / `per_page` after filtering.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires core classes; instantiate only via `edminboost_anm_run_plugin()`.
- `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin` constructor: `Admin`, `Notices`, `Interceptor`, `Ajax`, `Digest`, `Ad_Redirects`.
- Domain helpers (static or instantiated as needed): `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Rules`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Stats`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Importer`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ad_Redirects` (URL normalize/match helpers).
- Activation seeds options via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Activator`; deactivation clears digest schedule.

## Settings Option Shape (top-level keys)

```php
array(
	'enabled'                              => false,
	'hide_core_notices'                    => false,
	'manage_notices_mode'                  => 'hide_selected', // show_all | hide_all | hide_selected | compact_panel
	'disable_plugin_update_notifications'  => false,
	'disable_core_update_notifications'    => false,
	'show_hidden_notices_in_toolbar'       => false,
	'standard_admin_notices'               => array( /* per-level handling */ ),
	'non_standard_admin_notices'           => array(
		'no_level'             => 'inbox',
		'css_ignore_selectors' => '',
	),
	'hiding_notifications'                 => array( 'mode' => 'all', 'users' => array() ),
	'acl'                                  => array( 'roles' => array() ),
	'notice_panel'                         => array(
		'enabled'     => true,
		'style'       => 'link',       // link | bell_link | dropdown | dropdown_compact
		'position'    => 'default',    // see get_notice_panel_position_slugs()
		'badge_style' => 'count',      // count | count_9plus | count_99plus | dot | dot_pulse | none
		'colors'      => array( /* badge, badge_text, accent, accent_hover, bell_active */ ),
	),
	'upsell_preset'     => array( 'enabled' => false, 'custom_phrases' => array() ),
	'safety_guard'      => array( 'enabled' => true, 'mode' => 'strict' ),
	'client_shield'     => array( 'enabled' => false, 'roles' => array( ... ) ),
	'digest'            => array(
		'enabled'                => false,
		'recipients'             => 'admin@...',
		'subject'                => '',  // empty = default; supports {site_name}
		'intro'                  => '',
		'include_stats'          => true,
		'include_recent_notices' => true,
		'recent_notices_count'   => 10,  // clamped 1–25 in sanitize
		'footer'                 => '',
	),
	'webhook'           => array(
		'enabled' => false,
		'url'     => '',
		'message' => '',  // empty = default template; token placeholders in EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook
	),
	'word_filters'      => array( 'spam_words' => array(), 'whitelist_words' => array() ),
	'block_ad_redirects'=> array( 'enabled' => false, 'urls' => array() ),
)
```

Separate options: `RULES_OPTION` (rule list), `INBOX_OPTION` (captured notices), `STATS_OPTION` (counters).

## Partials

| Partial | Context |
|---------|---------|
| `edminboost-anm-dashboard-page.php` | Dashboard stats + quick actions |
| `edminboost-anm-inbox-page.php` | Inbox list table shell |
| `edminboost-anm-inbox-table-rows.php` | Inbox `<tr>` fragment (page + AJAX) |
| `edminboost-anm-rules-page.php` | Rules + WP preset conversion |
| `edminboost-anm-settings-page.php` | Settings API form |
| `edminboost-anm-notice-panel-dropdown.php` | Admin bar dropdown preview |

`EDMINBOOST_ANM_Notices::DROPDOWN_PREVIEW_LIMIT` (8) caps dropdown preview items.

- Settings help tips: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::help_tip( $message, $placement = 'below' )` — escaped dashicons + `data-tip` + `data-tip-placement` (`below`|`left`) for JS popup; output is safe HTML (escape in helper, document phpcs ignore when echoing in partials).
- Notice panel: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::get_notice_panel_*()` registries; `get_notice_panel_admin_bar_placement()`, `get_notice_panel_preview_layout()`, `notice_panel_style_is_dropdown()`, `notice_panel_style_uses_bell()`, `format_notice_panel_badge_display_count()`, etc. `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Notices::build_notice_badge_markup()` mirrors badge rules for live admin bar.
- Digest: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Digest::build_email_content()`, `format_email_body_plain()`, `build_email()`, `get_preview()` (includes structured `content` + plain `body`), `get_recipients()`, `SITE_NAME_TOKEN`; filter `edminboost_anm_digest_email`.
- Webhook: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook::build_payload()`, `build_message_text()`, `get_preview()`, `get_preview_notice()`, `get_sample_notice()`; filter `edminboost_anm_webhook_payload`.
- Sanitize helpers: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize_digest_settings()`, `sanitize_webhook_settings()` (Settings API save; digest preview uses full digest sanitizer; webhook preview AJAX sanitizes `message` only).

- Document `@var` annotations at the top of partials.
- Prefix partial-local variables with `$edminboost_anm_` to avoid collisions.

## Docblocks

Document all public methods with `@param`, `@return`, and `@var` on class properties.
